menu "Denon/Spotify Controller"

menu "Phase 0 spike"

config DSC_SPIKE_WIFI_SSID
    string "WiFi SSID for the Phase 0 spike"
    default ""
    help
        The spike needs a real AP so WiFi DMA contends with the LCD scanout.
        Without it the R1 numbers are optimistic and must not be trusted.
        Environment, not code -- set it here rather than editing main.c.

config DSC_SPIKE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "WiFi password for the Phase 0 spike"
    default ""

config DSC_SPIKE_URL
    string "HTTPS URL to download once per spike run"
    default "https://ash-speed.hetzner.com/100MB.bin"
    help
        Fetched ONCE per run, as a bounded Range request (see
        SPIKE_NET_RANGE_BYTES in spike_net_load.c), not in a loop. A tiny
        page (the old default, google.com) finishes instantly and measures
        nothing -- but so does hammering the same host with a fresh TLS
        handshake every couple of seconds for the whole run: real bring-up
        on hardware showed a public bandwidth-test host dropping or 429-ing
        every connection but the last when hit that way. One real,
        sustained connection is both more realistic (an OTA/artwork fetch
        is a single request, not a poll loop) and reliable.

endmenu

config DSC_FACTORY_TEST
    bool "Build factory test mode instead of the application"
    default n
    help
        Manufacturing hardware exerciser (docs/SECURITY.md §7b). Must never
        be enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set.

endmenu
